data.content:
## What Breaks in .NET 11

In EF Core 11 (ships with .NET 11), the **Cosmos DB provider removes the sync-over-async opt-in entirely**. The `EnableSyncOverAsync()` configuration option you used in .NET 10 no longer exists.

All synchronous LINQ operators (`ToList()`, `First()`, `Count()`) and `SaveChanges()` now throw an **`InvalidOperationException`** at runtime with no workaround.

## The Fix

Convert to async throughout:

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

**Summary of the timeline:**
| Version | Behavior |
|---------|----------|
| .NET 9 | Sync-over-async worked but logged warnings |
| .NET 10 | Threw by default; `EnableSyncOverAsync()` opt-in available |
| .NET 11 | Opt-in removed; sync calls always throw |

You'll need to propagate `async`/`await` up through your call stack (controllers, services, etc.) — there's no way to keep synchronous Cosmos queries in EF Core 11.
